<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niall Glúndub</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 919</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Niall mac Áeda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niall Glúndub was a king of Ailech from the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-king-of-ireland">High King of Ireland</a> from 916. One of the most powerful Irish kings of his time, he led a campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> who had re-established themselves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> and was killed fighting them at the Battle of Islandbridge in 919. The O'Neill family takes its name from him.</p></div>
